BManx2000 wrote:
> Ben Kimball wrote:
>
> > Zubin XIX (it's a good thing his family has a rule about having kids before
> > questing) is on the Minetown level. He's a chaotic elven wizard, and there's
> > a chaotic altar in the town.
>
> > Is it a good idea to kill all the guards and sacrifice their elven bodies on
> > the altar? He hasn't received any gifts from his deity yet.
>
> Considering that the watchmen are in fact human, nothing bad will happen
> from sacrificing them. However, you will take a BIG alignment hit from
> killing the watchmen. According to the myths and facts spoiler, the
> penalty for killing a monster that is always created peaceful (like the
> watchmen) carries a penalty of -15. I tested this and it seems to apply
> even to chaotics. So unless you are sure that your alignment is in the
> hundreds, I would advise against it.

The alignment penalty is based on your diety's viewpoint not
yours.  Killing peacefulls means killing fellow followers of
your dieties.  Dieties like having followers so they aren't
happy with having theirs wiped out.  Thus even a chaotic
gets a small penalty from killing peacefulls.

Playing chaotic means less penalty for killing peacefull @'s.
The watchmen have plenty of equipment that you might want.
In particular a wizard will want studded leather armor, leather
gloves and high boots before better armor is collected later
in the game.  Plus the watch captain has 50-50 chance silver
saber of long sword which make for acceptible backup melee
weapons for a pre-artifact wizard.

If you haven't received any artifacts yet and the altar is
already co-aligned you don't need to worry about the alignment
penalty.  Offering and/or killing more hostiles will handle
that and you want your first artifact so the more bodies the
better.

My conclusion - If you are certain you will survive the
attack, patiently herd the watchmen into rooms, lock the
doors, and then attack them one by one.  Watchmen will open
unlocked doors but they don't have key so they are easy to
lock up.  Kill them, sac them, check their stuff for b/u/c,
try on all that isn't cursed, keep the best of the lot.
The mines supply a LOT of metal armor items and a spell
caster like a wizard will want the leather equipment
carried by the watch.



